    "updated_at": "2022-12-14T02:44:00Z",
    "body": "> I don't understand why we'd restrict promises from being held by these types.\r\n\r\nI was thinking that in the absence of a definite use case, the added complexity of specifying the constraints right wouldn’t be worthwhile — shouldn’t `FrozenArray<Promise<SomeDictionary>>` be invalid just as `FrozenArray<SomeDictionary>` should be? But it’s true that e.g. `FrozenArray<Promise<SomeInterface>>` wouldn’t be problematic, it’s just not clear to me when it would have any utility.",
